<title>FRANCE: EU sells German intervention rye, rejects barley.</title>
<headline>EU sells German intervention rye, rejects barley.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday sold 13,716 tonnes of German intervention rye for export to countries outside the EU, EU grain officials said.</p>
<p>But the EU's cereals management committee in Brussels rejected all bids to export German intervention barley, they said.  </p>
<p>The EU sold the German intervention rye at 103.52 Ecus per tonne, the officials later specified.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
